---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import Header from "../components/base/Header.astro";
import Footer from "../components/base/Footer.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Terms of Service"
  description="Review the terms governing reservations, payments, vehicle rentals, website use, and services provided by 305Fleet in South Florida."
  noindex={false}
  hideSpanishHreflang={true}
  xDefaultOverride="https://305fleet.com/terms-of-service/"
>
  <Header />

  <main id="main-content" class="flex-1 bg-white">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-4 py-12 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 lg:py-16">
      <h1 class="text-3xl font-bold text-gray-900 sm:text-4xl">305Fleet Terms of Service</h1>
      <p class="mt-3 text-sm font-medium text-brand-300 uppercase tracking-wide">Effective Date: September 15, 2026</p>

      <div class="mt-8 prose prose-sm prose-gray max-w-none">
        <p>
          These Terms of Service (&ldquo;Terms&rdquo;) govern your use of 305fleet.com, reservations made with Turomina LLC dba 305Fleet, and related services provided by 305Fleet (&ldquo;305Fleet,&rdquo; &ldquo;we,&rdquo; &ldquo;us,&rdquo; or &ldquo;our&rdquo;).
        </p>
        <p>
          By accessing our website, submitting a reservation request, completing a booking, electronically accepting these Terms, or using our services, you agree to be bound by these Terms.
        </p>
        <p>
          If you do not agree to these Terms, do not complete a reservation or use our rental services.
        </p>

        <div class="not-prose mt-6 mb-8 rounded-lg border border-brand-100 bg-brand-50 p-4 text-sm text-brand-700">
          <p class="font-semibold text-brand mb-1">305Fleet</p>
          <p>Turomina LLC dba 305Fleet</p>
          <p>Pembroke Pines, Florida</p>
          <p>Phone: <a href="tel:+13054391247" class="text-brand underline hover:text-brand-400">305-439-1247</a></p>
          <p>Email: <a href="mailto:turohost@305fleet.com" class="text-brand underline hover:text-brand-400">turohost@305fleet.com</a></p>
          <p>Website: <a href="https://305fleet.com" class="text-brand underline hover:text-brand-400">305fleet.com</a></p>
        </div>

        <div class="not-prose mb-8 rounded-lg border border-accent-100 bg-accent-50 p-4 text-sm text-gray-700">
          <p>
            By completing a reservation, you agree to the 305Fleet Terms of Service, Rules of the Road, and applicable Vehicle Rental Agreement.
          </p>
        </div>

        <h2>1. Terms That Apply to Your Rental</h2>
        <p>
          These Terms govern the website, booking process, reservations, payments, communications, and general services provided by 305Fleet.
        </p>
        <p>
          Each vehicle rental is also governed by the applicable:
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li>305Fleet Vehicle Rental Agreement;</li>
          <li>confirmed Wheelbase reservation and Reservation Receipt;</li>
          <li>305Fleet Rules of the Road;</li>
          <li>checkout and check-in records;</li>
          <li>vehicle-specific instructions or disclosures;</li>
          <li>applicable insurance or protection-plan terms; and</li>
          <li>written amendments or special terms agreed to by 305Fleet and the renter.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          These documents collectively form the agreement applicable to the rental.
        </p>
        <p>
          If a reservation-specific term shown on a confirmed reservation conflicts with these Terms, the reservation-specific term controls as to that particular item.
        </p>
        <p>
          If these Terms conflict with the Vehicle Rental Agreement regarding possession, operation, authorized drivers, vehicle condition, damage, insurance, prohibited use, geographic restrictions, vehicle recovery, or return of the vehicle, the Vehicle Rental Agreement controls.
        </p>

        <h2>2. Eligibility to Rent</h2>
        <p>
          To rent a vehicle from 305Fleet, you must:
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li>be legally capable of entering into a binding contract;</li>
          <li>meet the minimum age requirement applicable to the reservation;</li>
          <li>possess a valid, unexpired driver&rsquo;s license acceptable for the rental;</li>
          <li>complete any required identity and driver verification;</li>
          <li>meet applicable insurance or protection requirements;</li>
          <li>provide accurate and complete information; and</li>
          <li>provide a valid payment method accepted by the booking platform.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          All authorized drivers must independently satisfy applicable driver eligibility requirements.
        </p>
        <p>
          305Fleet may decline or cancel a reservation where eligibility, identity verification, driver&rsquo;s-license verification, payment, fraud-prevention, insurance, protection, security, or other reasonable rental requirements are not satisfied.
        </p>

        <h2>3. Driver&rsquo;s License Verification</h2>
        <p>
          Florida law requires a vehicle renter to be duly licensed.
        </p>
        <p>
          305Fleet or its authorized service provider may inspect, electronically verify, or otherwise validate a renter&rsquo;s driver&rsquo;s license and confirm that it is unexpired before allowing possession of a vehicle.
        </p>
        <p>
          By booking with 305Fleet, you authorize reasonable driver&rsquo;s-license and identity verification for purposes of determining rental eligibility and preventing fraud.
        </p>

        <h2>4. Reservations</h2>
        <p>
          305Fleet currently uses Wheelbase and may use other authorized third-party platforms or service providers to process reservations.
        </p>
        <p>
          A reservation is not final until it has been confirmed through the applicable booking system and all required payment, verification, documentation, deposit, and electronic-signature requirements have been completed.
        </p>
        <p>
          Reservation-specific information may include:
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li>vehicle;</li>
          <li>pickup and return dates and times;</li>
          <li>rental price;</li>
          <li>mileage allowance;</li>
          <li>taxes and fees;</li>
          <li>security deposit;</li>
          <li>delivery or pickup charges;</li>
          <li>add-ons;</li>
          <li>insurance or protection selection; and</li>
          <li>other reservation-specific terms.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          The confirmed reservation and Reservation Receipt are incorporated into the rental transaction.
        </p>

        <h2>5. Accuracy of Information</h2>
        <p>
          You agree to provide truthful, complete, current, and accurate information throughout the booking and rental process.
        </p>
        <p>
          This includes information concerning your:
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li>identity;</li>
          <li>driver&rsquo;s license;</li>
          <li>address;</li>
          <li>date of birth;</li>
          <li>telephone number;</li>
          <li>email address;</li>
          <li>payment method;</li>
          <li>insurance;</li>
          <li>additional drivers; and</li>
          <li>other information reasonably required for the rental.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          Providing materially false, misleading, fraudulent, incomplete, or unauthorized information may result in rejection or cancellation of the reservation, refusal to release the vehicle, termination of the rental, recovery of the vehicle, denial of future rentals, or other remedies permitted by law or the Vehicle Rental Agreement.
        </p>

        <h2>6. Pricing</h2>
        <p>
          Rental pricing is based on the price displayed or confirmed for the applicable reservation.
        </p>
        <p>
          Rates may vary based on:
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li>vehicle;</li>
          <li>rental dates;</li>
          <li>rental duration;</li>
          <li>demand;</li>
          <li>season;</li>
          <li>pickup or delivery location;</li>
          <li>mileage;</li>
          <li>add-ons;</li>
          <li>insurance or protection products;</li>
          <li>taxes;</li>
          <li>fees; and</li>
          <li>other reservation-specific factors.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          305Fleet may change pricing for future reservations at any time before a reservation is confirmed.
        </p>
        <p>
          Once confirmed, the applicable reservation price will control, subject to approved modifications, extensions, additional usage, additional services, penalties, damage, mileage, fuel or charging shortages, tolls, violations, or other properly chargeable amounts.
        </p>

        <h2>7. Payment Authorization</h2>
        <p>
          By completing a reservation, you authorize 305Fleet and its authorized booking and payment providers to charge the payment method associated with your reservation for amounts properly due under the reservation, these Terms, or the Vehicle Rental Agreement.
        </p>
        <p>
          Such charges may include, where applicable:
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li>rental charges;</li>
          <li>taxes and fees;</li>
          <li>security deposits;</li>
          <li>delivery charges;</li>
          <li>add-ons;</li>
          <li>rental extensions;</li>
          <li>excess mileage;</li>
          <li>fuel or charging shortages;</li>
          <li>late-return charges;</li>
          <li>cleaning charges;</li>
          <li>smoking or vaping charges;</li>
          <li>tolls;</li>
          <li>parking charges;</li>
          <li>citations and violations;</li>
          <li>towing and impound charges;</li>
          <li>lost keys or equipment;</li>
          <li>insurance or protection deductibles;</li>
          <li>vehicle damage;</li>
          <li>vehicle recovery expenses;</li>
          <li>administrative charges permitted under the rental documents; and</li>
          <li>other documented amounts properly owed under the rental agreement.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          Some amounts may be charged after the rental ends if the applicable expense, toll, citation, damage, claim, or other obligation becomes known later.
        </p>

        <h2>8. Security Deposits</h2>
        <p>
          305Fleet may require a security deposit.
        </p>
        <p>
          The amount, if applicable, will be disclosed in connection with the reservation.
        </p>
        <p>
          A security deposit may be held and applied to amounts properly owed by the renter, including:
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li>vehicle damage;</li>
          <li>deductibles;</li>
          <li>excess mileage;</li>
          <li>missing fuel or battery charge;</li>
          <li>tolls;</li>
          <li>violations;</li>
          <li>extraordinary cleaning;</li>
          <li>smoking or vaping;</li>
          <li>missing equipment;</li>
          <li>late-return charges; and</li>
          <li>other amounts authorized under the Vehicle Rental Agreement.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          Any remaining refundable amount will be released or refunded through the applicable payment processor.
        </p>
        <p>
          The time required for a released authorization or refund to appear in a renter&rsquo;s account may depend on the renter&rsquo;s bank, card issuer, or payment provider.
        </p>

        <h2>9. Cancellation and Refunds</h2>
        <p>
          The cancellation and refund policy displayed through Wheelbase or the applicable booking system at the time a reservation is confirmed governs that reservation.
        </p>
        <p>
          Cancellation terms may vary depending on the vehicle, booking date, rental date, reservation channel, or other booking conditions.
        </p>
        <p>
          Certain charges may be non-refundable as disclosed during booking.
        </p>
        <p>
          An early vehicle return does not create a right to a refund unless the applicable booking policy expressly provides otherwise or 305Fleet agrees otherwise in writing.
        </p>

        <h2>10. Reservation Changes</h2>
        <p>
          Reservation changes are subject to availability and 305Fleet approval.
        </p>
        <p>
          Changes may affect:
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li>price;</li>
          <li>mileage allowance;</li>
          <li>security deposit;</li>
          <li>taxes;</li>
          <li>fees;</li>
          <li>insurance or protection charges;</li>
          <li>delivery charges; and</li>
          <li>other reservation terms.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          A requested change is not effective until confirmed through Wheelbase or otherwise approved in writing by 305Fleet.
        </p>

        <h2>11. Rental Extensions</h2>
        <p>
          A renter may not retain a vehicle beyond the confirmed return date and time without prior approval from 305Fleet.
        </p>
        <p>
          Extension requests must be approved before the existing rental period expires.
        </p>
        <p>
          Submitting an extension request does not constitute approval.
        </p>
        <p>
          Continued possession of a vehicle does not automatically extend the rental.
        </p>
        <p>
          Approved extensions may result in additional rental charges, taxes, fees, protection charges, deposits, or other applicable costs.
        </p>

        <h2>12. Authorized Drivers</h2>
        <p>
          Only drivers who are listed, approved, and verified for the applicable reservation may operate a 305Fleet vehicle.
        </p>
        <p>
          The renter may not allow any other person to drive the vehicle.
        </p>
        <p>
          Allowing an unauthorized driver to operate the vehicle constitutes a material violation of the rental requirements and may affect insurance or protection coverage.
        </p>
        <p>
          Additional requirements governing authorized drivers are contained in the Vehicle Rental Agreement.
        </p>

        <h2>13. Insurance and Protection</h2>
        <p>
          Each reservation must satisfy the insurance or protection requirements applicable to that rental before the vehicle is released.
        </p>
        <p>
          Depending on the reservation, coverage may be satisfied through one of the following arrangements:
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li>a protection or insurance product selected through Wheelbase or another approved provider; or</li>
          <li>qualifying personal automobile insurance or other coverage accepted and verified for the reservation.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          If the renter selects a Wheelbase or other third-party protection or insurance product, that coverage is governed exclusively by the applicable provider&rsquo;s terms, conditions, exclusions, limits, deductibles, eligibility requirements, and claims procedures.
        </p>
        <p>
          305Fleet does not modify, expand, guarantee, or independently interpret coverage provided by Wheelbase, Outdoorsy, an insurer, credit-card issuer, protection provider, or other third party.
        </p>
        <p>
          If the renter declines an available protection or insurance product and instead relies on personal automobile insurance or other coverage, 305Fleet may require verification that such coverage applies to the rental vehicle and satisfies the requirements applicable to the reservation.
        </p>
        <p>
          Verification may be performed by Wheelbase, 305Fleet, the renter&rsquo;s insurer, a credit-card benefit administrator, or another authorized provider.
        </p>
        <p>
          Acceptance of a renter&rsquo;s personal insurance or other coverage does not guarantee payment of a claim.
        </p>
        <p>
          The renter remains responsible for any deductible, exclusion, limitation, denial of coverage, uncovered loss, prohibited use, unauthorized driver, or other amount for which the renter is responsible under the Vehicle Rental Agreement.
        </p>
        <p>
          Where the renter&rsquo;s own liability insurance and personal injury protection coverage are intended to be primary for a particular rental, the applicable Vehicle Rental Agreement will contain any notice required by Florida law.
        </p>
        <p>
          Selection of any insurance or protection option does not eliminate the renter&rsquo;s obligation to comply with the Vehicle Rental Agreement, Rules of the Road, or applicable coverage requirements.
        </p>

        <h2>14. Rules of the Road</h2>
        <p>
          All renters and authorized drivers must comply with the 305Fleet Rules of the Road provided during the reservation process.
        </p>
        <p>
          The Rules of the Road include requirements concerning matters such as:
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li>smoking and vaping;</li>
          <li>pets;</li>
          <li>authorized drivers;</li>
          <li>safe vehicle operation;</li>
          <li>prohibited uses;</li>
          <li>vehicle cleanliness;</li>
          <li>fuel or battery charge;</li>
          <li>tolls and parking;</li>
          <li>airport procedures;</li>
          <li>lockbox procedures;</li>
          <li>accidents;</li>
          <li>vehicle damage; and</li>
          <li>mechanical issues.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          Violation of the Rules of the Road may result in charges, termination of the rental, loss or denial of applicable protection, vehicle recovery, or other remedies where permitted by the Vehicle Rental Agreement and applicable law.
        </p>

        <h2>15. No Smoking or Vaping</h2>
        <p>
          Smoking or vaping of any kind is prohibited in all 305Fleet vehicles.
        </p>
        <p>
          This includes cigarettes, cigars, marijuana, vaping products, and other smoke- or vapor-producing products.
        </p>
        <p>
          Vehicles may be equipped with electronic smoking-detection technology.
        </p>
        <p>
          A $250 smoking/vaping fee may be charged for each reasonably documented smoking or vaping incident unless a different amount is expressly disclosed for the reservation.
        </p>

        <h2>16. Pets</h2>
        <p>
          Pets are not permitted unless approved by 305Fleet in advance or otherwise required by applicable law.
        </p>
        <p>
          The vehicle must be returned free from excessive pet hair, stains, odors, waste, damage, or other pet-related conditions requiring extraordinary cleaning or repair.
        </p>
        <p>
          Nothing in these Terms is intended to restrict rights provided under applicable service-animal or disability law.
        </p>

        <h2>17. Vehicle Cleanliness</h2>
        <p>
          Normal vehicle use is expected and does not require the renter to professionally clean the vehicle.
        </p>
        <p>
          However, a renter may be responsible for extraordinary cleaning reasonably required because of conditions beyond normal use, including excessive:
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li>dirt;</li>
          <li>sand;</li>
          <li>stains;</li>
          <li>spills;</li>
          <li>smoke residue or odor;</li>
          <li>pet hair;</li>
          <li>food or beverage residue;</li>
          <li>biological material; or</li>
          <li>other unusual contamination.</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>18. Prohibited Use</h2>
        <p>
          A 305Fleet vehicle may not be used for:
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li>illegal activity;</li>
          <li>operation while impaired by alcohol, drugs, medication, or another impairing substance;</li>
          <li>racing;</li>
          <li>speed contests;</li>
          <li>reckless driving;</li>
          <li>burnouts;</li>
          <li>drifting;</li>
          <li>stunts;</li>
          <li>unauthorized off-road use;</li>
          <li>unauthorized towing;</li>
          <li>rideshare, delivery, courier, or commercial transportation unless specifically authorized;</li>
          <li>operation by an unauthorized driver;</li>
          <li>sub-rental;</li>
          <li>intentional abuse or misuse;</li>
          <li>unauthorized repair or modification;</li>
          <li>tampering with tracking, telematics, smoking-detection, or security equipment; or</li>
          <li>other use prohibited by the Vehicle Rental Agreement.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          Material prohibited use may result in termination of the rental, vehicle recovery, additional charges, loss or denial of applicable insurance or protection benefits, and financial responsibility for resulting losses.
        </p>

        <h2>19. Geographic Restrictions</h2>
        <p>
          Unless 305Fleet provides prior written authorization, vehicles may be operated only within the geographic area permitted by the Vehicle Rental Agreement.
        </p>
        <p>
          A vehicle may not be taken outside an authorized area simply because navigation software, a booking platform, or another system permits the route.
        </p>
        <p>
          Unauthorized travel may constitute a material breach of the rental agreement.
        </p>

        <h2>20. Vehicle Availability</h2>
        <p>
          305Fleet makes reasonable efforts to provide the vehicle reserved.
        </p>
        <p>
          A specific vehicle may become unavailable due to:
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li>an accident;</li>
          <li>mechanical failure;</li>
          <li>delayed return by a prior renter;</li>
          <li>theft;</li>
          <li>maintenance;</li>
          <li>manufacturer recall;</li>
          <li>safety concerns; or</li>
          <li>circumstances outside 305Fleet&rsquo;s reasonable control.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          If the reserved vehicle becomes unavailable, 305Fleet may attempt to provide a comparable substitute.
        </p>
        <p>
          If no reasonable substitute is available, 305Fleet may cancel the affected reservation and refund amounts collected for the unavailable rental as appropriate.
        </p>
        <p>
          To the fullest extent permitted by law, 305Fleet is not responsible for consequential travel expenses arising solely from vehicle unavailability, including hotel costs, airfare, missed events, or alternative transportation expenses.
        </p>

        <h2>21. Vehicle Condition and Inspection</h2>
        <p>
          Vehicle condition may be documented before and after a rental using:
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li>Wheelbase checkout and check-in records;</li>
          <li>photographs;</li>
          <li>video;</li>
          <li>odometer readings;</li>
          <li>fuel or battery readings;</li>
          <li>inspection records;</li>
          <li>telematics;</li>
          <li>written notes; and</li>
          <li>other reasonable documentation.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          The renter should inspect the vehicle at pickup and promptly identify material pre-existing damage not shown in the checkout record.
        </p>
        <p>
          The Vehicle Rental Agreement governs responsibility for damage occurring during the rental.
        </p>

        <h2>22. Fuel and Electric Vehicle Charging</h2>
        <p>
          The vehicle must be returned with the fuel level or battery state of charge required by the reservation or checkout record unless different written instructions are provided.
        </p>
        <p>
          If returned below the required level, the renter may be responsible for the reasonable cost of restoring the fuel or charge together with an applicable disclosed service fee.
        </p>
        <p>
          Renters of electric or plug-in hybrid vehicles are responsible for maintaining sufficient battery charge to operate and return the vehicle safely.
        </p>

        <h2>23. Mileage</h2>
        <p>
          The mileage allowance applicable to the rental is the allowance shown in the reservation, vehicle listing, or related booking materials.
        </p>
        <p>
          Mileage exceeding the allowance may result in an excess-mileage charge at the rate applicable to the reservation.
        </p>
        <p>
          Mileage may be verified using odometer readings, Wheelbase records, vehicle telematics, or other reasonable records.
        </p>

        <h2>24. Tolls, Parking, Tickets, and Violations</h2>
        <p>
          The renter is responsible for costs attributable to possession or use of the vehicle during the rental period, including:
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li>tolls;</li>
          <li>parking charges;</li>
          <li>traffic citations;</li>
          <li>parking citations;</li>
          <li>red-light camera violations;</li>
          <li>towing;</li>
          <li>impound costs;</li>
          <li>airport parking; and</li>
          <li>other violations or charges.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          Some charges may not be received until after the rental ends.
        </p>
        <p>
          305Fleet may charge properly documented amounts and any applicable administrative processing charge permitted by the rental documents and applicable law.
        </p>

        <h2>25. Airport Pickup and Return</h2>
        <p>
          When a rental involves airport delivery or return, the renter must follow 305Fleet&rsquo;s written pickup and return instructions.
        </p>
        <p>
          Instructions may address:
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li>airport or parking facility;</li>
          <li>garage;</li>
          <li>level;</li>
          <li>row or zone;</li>
          <li>parking space;</li>
          <li>photographs;</li>
          <li>parking tickets;</li>
          <li>keys;</li>
          <li>protective pouches;</li>
          <li>lockboxes; and</li>
          <li>return procedures.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          Renters may be responsible for airport parking charges as disclosed in connection with the reservation.
        </p>
        <p>
          A renter may also be responsible for charges resulting from incorrect or unauthorized parking, including additional parking, towing, citations, or reasonable vehicle-recovery costs.
        </p>

        <h2>26. GPS, Telematics, and Vehicle Technology</h2>
        <p>
          305Fleet vehicles may contain GPS, telematics, diagnostic, smoking-detection, remote-security, and other fleet-management technology.
        </p>
        <p>
          305Fleet may use these systems for legitimate business purposes including:
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li>theft prevention;</li>
          <li>vehicle recovery;</li>
          <li>locating overdue or unreturned vehicles;</li>
          <li>fleet security;</li>
          <li>mileage verification;</li>
          <li>maintenance;</li>
          <li>diagnostics;</li>
          <li>investigation of unauthorized or prohibited use;</li>
          <li>geographic compliance; and</li>
          <li>protection of 305Fleet property.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          Renters may not disable, remove, disconnect, obstruct, alter, or tamper with authorized tracking, telematics, security, or vehicle-management equipment.
        </p>
        <p>
          Additional disclosures concerning these systems are contained in the Vehicle Rental Agreement.
        </p>

        <h2>27. Accidents, Damage, Theft, and Mechanical Problems</h2>
        <p>
          The renter must contact 305Fleet promptly in the event of:
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li>an accident;</li>
          <li>collision;</li>
          <li>vehicle damage;</li>
          <li>theft;</li>
          <li>vandalism;</li>
          <li>warning light;</li>
          <li>flat tire;</li>
          <li>breakdown; or</li>
          <li>significant mechanical problem.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          The renter must not continue operating a vehicle when continued operation may be unsafe or may reasonably cause additional damage.
        </p>
        <p>
          The Vehicle Rental Agreement contains additional accident-reporting, police-report, documentation, insurance, repair, and cooperation requirements.
        </p>

        <h2>28. Vehicle Return</h2>
        <p>
          The vehicle must be returned at the date, time, location, and in the manner required by the reservation and written return instructions.
        </p>
        <p>
          The renter remains responsible for the vehicle until it has been properly returned and secured in accordance with the applicable procedure.
        </p>
        <p>
          A renter must promptly notify 305Fleet if circumstances prevent proper return.
        </p>

        <h2>29. Late or Unreturned Vehicles</h2>
        <p>
          Keeping a vehicle beyond the authorized rental period without approval is prohibited.
        </p>
        <p>
          Late charges or additional rental amounts may apply as provided by the Vehicle Rental Agreement.
        </p>
        <p>
          If a vehicle is materially overdue and the renter cannot be reached, 305Fleet may take reasonable lawful measures to locate and recover the vehicle.
        </p>
        <p>
          Where appropriate under the circumstances and permitted by law, an unreturned vehicle may be reported to law enforcement.
        </p>

        <h2>30. Lost Keys and Equipment</h2>
